{"data": [{"author_id": "1788914648172916736", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:06:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510349955875272"], "id": "2118510349955875272", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus AI speeding up AI research is the loop.\nSame loop for game assets: agent → 3D mesh → drop in Studio.\nThe bottleneck moved from modeling to taste.", "url": "https://x.com/Waspesai/status/2118510349955875272"}, {"author_id": "1928472777750884352", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:41:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118504003453759902"], "id": "2118504003453759902", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1524764097841094660", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118426535296381234", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@notjazii @kimmonismus It's fine lets accelerate", "url": "https://x.com/Thirumagal_12/status/2118504003453759902"}, {"author_id": "1673777719404818433", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:29:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118500903711854799"], "id": "2118500903711854799", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus If METR's 2x is right, the compounding is the story, not the headline number. AI speeding up AI research means each generation doesn't just get better — it arrives faster, and the gap between labs that can harness that loop and those that can't widens with every cycle.\n\nThe", "url": "https://x.com/MichaelGHash/status/2118500903711854799"}, {"author_id": "1142469860", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:48:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118475556077416881"], "id": "2118475556077416881", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Wasn’t all this obvious development from the shift to scion?", "url": "https://x.com/KellerZoe/status/2118475556077416881"}, {"author_id": "1330927102187724805", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:11:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466156621443196"], "id": "2118466156621443196", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus La parte más interesante: no es solo más GPUs. Es IA acelerando la propia investigación de Anthropic. Cuando el lab usa sus modelos para mejorar los siguientes, el loop se cierra. ¿Cuánto de ese 1.9x es ya AI-on-AI?", "url": "https://x.com/EndroCb/status/2118466156621443196"}, {"author_id": "2102318912625094656", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:54:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118461963655348578"], "id": "2118461963655348578", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The tricky part will be untangling synthetic data gains from actual agentic R&amp;D assistance, since the compute costs and feedback loops for those two look completely different.", "url": "https://x.com/JohnKocdr/status/2118461963655348578"}, {"author_id": "1483051266", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:46:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118459975802724410"], "id": "2118459975802724410", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 112, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus How much of the research can their models actually do on their own now?", "url": "https://x.com/TheElliottSmith/status/2118459975802724410"}, {"author_id": "1994706437646553089", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:30:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118456023107436589"], "id": "2118456023107436589", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 66, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus They better release a huge breakthrough that truly benefits humanity or they’re cooked", "url": "https://x.com/JoeWilliams010/status/2118456023107436589"}, {"author_id": "1347000683850059776", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:58:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118447987907276956"], "id": "2118447987907276956", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 1.9x acceleration from using their own models. feedback loop is real", "url": "https://x.com/vibecodeceo/status/2118447987907276956"}, {"author_id": "2110982355817218048", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:57:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118447611338527131"], "id": "2118447611338527131", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The saturation caveat is the part to watch. Model 4 is above 50% on every AECI benchmark tested, yet the estimate still comes out at 1.9x after dropping benchmarks past 85%.", "url": "https://x.com/hoppangdev/status/2118447611338527131"}, {"author_id": "2103389296145448960", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:54:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118446832787550579"], "id": "2118446832787550579", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus If AI is now a large part of Anthropic's own acceleration, the bottleneck shifts from research headcount to eval quality and data flywheels. Does 1.9x hold once the easy self-improvement loops saturate?", "url": "https://x.com/Aistarjohn/status/2118446832787550579"}, {"author_id": "2066467180091494400", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:45:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118444561311875370"], "id": "2118444561311875370", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Read More: https://t.co/oh5KNJB3gv", "url": "https://x.com/CryptoBella365/status/2118444561311875370"}, {"author_id": "2117711508100501505", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:44:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118444308433150255"], "id": "2118444308433150255", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 89, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Everyone's reading this as \"AI builds AI, humans optional.\"\n\nLook closer. ~80% of the speedup is AI helping researchers. People still steer it.\n\nHuman + AI beats AI alone. That gap is where the value lives. https://t.co/Y6RMvtjNqF", "url": "https://x.com/TimmyGack/status/2118444308433150255"}, {"author_id": "2050045441081823232", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:37:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118442645165154410"], "id": "2118442645165154410", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus AI accelerating AI progress is the feedback loop everyone predicted. Nearly 2x on independent evals makes it hard to dismiss as marketing.", "url": "https://x.com/abenezerNu/status/2118442645165154410"}, {"author_id": "941659902820438016", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:20:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118438390047588685"], "id": "2118438390047588685", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 99, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus I'd be interested in which research steps got faster. Generating experiments, running them and choosing what to pursue can each shorten a development cycle in very different ways.", "url": "https://x.com/tinkerlog/status/2118438390047588685"}, {"author_id": "2106189720678289408", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:14:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118436762276266183"], "id": "2118436762276266183", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus twice as fast sounds wild until you read the fine print. that 1.5x to 2.8x range is doing a lot of heavy lifting", "url": "https://x.com/weirdwavesu/status/2118436762276266183"}, {"author_id": "127042462", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:14:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118436714947514662"], "id": "2118436714947514662", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus If AI itself is driving most of that acceleration, the next year of Anthropic progress could look nothing like the last three.", "url": "https://x.com/Notorious_corbz/status/2118436714947514662"}, {"author_id": "1033891638140186625", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:12:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118436285962404106"], "id": "2118436285962404106", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Independent and METR in the same sentence is crazy", "url": "https://x.com/thalwain/status/2118436285962404106"}, {"author_id": "2036622572847337472", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:10:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118435796894064725"], "id": "2118435796894064725", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus ai is doing 80% of the work on the next ai now. the other 20% is someone clicking approve on the pr", "url": "https://x.com/bunker38222/status/2118435796894064725"}, {"author_id": "1708492008673722368", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:04:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118434198990319893"], "id": "2118434198990319893", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 268, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus That 80% estimate is wild if true.", "url": "https://x.com/annanidev/status/2118434198990319893"}, {"author_id": "328533041", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:04:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118434189317988859"], "id": "2118434189317988859", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Twice as fast just from using their own models is the bit every other lab has to answer to.", "url": "https://x.com/TomaszPabich/status/2118434189317988859"}, {"author_id": "1930087175745613827", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:01:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118433522285519138"], "id": "2118433522285519138", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118423591364546856", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 1.9倍先打个问号：95%置信区间宽到1.5-2.6倍，几乎等于没法定量。80%归因更来自员工自述访谈，主观性太强；METR还拿了Anthropic内部数据，独立性也要打问号。我的立场：加速属实，但幅度被夸大了。基准分增速能直接等同能力增速吗？", "url": "https://x.com/srduino2026/status/2118433522285519138"}, {"author_id": "1706504921271713792", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:00:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118433265258504482"], "id": 